# PIPELINE TEMPLATE LAW — Q&A GENERATION

**Status: MANDATORY · NON-NEGOTIABLE.** Applies to every new Q&A generated by the pipeline (`generateOne`, cloud writer, batch workflows).

## Golden template shape (read-only)

**Golden template law:** `GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_TOP10.md` · `GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_QA.md` — sole doc sources of truth; do not restate section orders here.

**Code audits:** `_ranking_top10_gold_template.js` · `_qa_gold_template.js`  
**Classify:** `pickGoldTemplate(id, body, title)` in `_pulse_gold_template_router.js` — **before** any draft; lock result; never switch mid-run.

---

## Pipeline steps (in order)

### STEP 1 — CLASSIFY

Call `pickGoldTemplate` **before** any draft write. Lock `template`, `goldId`, `goldUrl`, `reason`.

### STEP 2 — SEED

Assign id, pillar, question. Load the **locked** gold outline for the classified type (`QA_TEMPLATE_OUTLINE` or `TOP10_TEMPLATE_OUTLINE` from code modules).

### STEP 3 — GENERATE

Write **new** content into the classified template shape only. `generateOne` in `_scrub_button_server.js` is the canonical path.

**Do:** `seedWrite` → `fixEntry` → body conforms to locked outline in the MD spec + code audit. New copy + new images per entry.

**Do NOT:** regenerate/restyle gold template definitions; freestyle structure; prepend Q&A hero on Top 10; inject `@@PRODUCT` into Q&A; publish before 13/13.

### STEP 4 — SCORE + SURGICAL FIX

`entryScrubPipeline` / `gradeEntry` + `rubricSignOff` + gold audit (`auditQaGoldTemplate` or `auditTop10GoldTemplate`). Fix failing checkpoints only. Re-verify gold structure after every edit. Never merge template elements across types.

### STEP 5 — CERTIFY

**No draft publishes below 13/13.** Rubric: `SCRUBBER_SPEC.md`.

---

## RULES

1. Classification before generation — never mid-stream.
2. Exactly one template per entry — no hybrids.
3. Golden template **shape** is immutable; bypass only with owner passcode `4444`.
4. Surgical fixes only; re-verify template structure after every fix pass.
5. Publish gate: **13/13 only** (same rubric for generator and scrubber).

---

## Logging (every run)

1. **Classification** — `template`, `goldId`, `reason`
2. **Template used** — `top10` | `qa`
3. **Score history** — score after each pipeline round
4. **Final 13/13 proof** — gold audit + rubric compliant before certify

Helper: `_pipeline_template_log.js` → `makePipelineTemplateRun`.

---

